# MySlides Slide Design Schema

The AI generates slides in strict JSON. The frontend renders it. AI generates structure; the system guarantees beauty.

## Layouts (7)
- `title-only` - Opening, section headers, closing
- `title-content` - Standard content
- `two-column` - Compare/contrast, dual lists
- `text-cards` - Genspark-style: left=title+subtitle+body, right=4 numbered cards (content[0]=subtitle, [1]=body, [2..5]=cards)
- `section-header` - Section dividers
- `quote` - Quotes, testimonials
- `image-left` - Content left, image right (uses imageUrl)

## Animations
`none` | `fadeIn` | `titleThenBullets` | `slideFromRight` | `scaleIn`

## Background Styles
- `solid` - Clean content slides
- `gradient` - Requires `bgGradient` (CSS string)
- `image` - Requires `imagePrompt` (DALL-E generates)

## Schema Location
- `functions/src/slideDesignSchema.ts` - Canonical schema
- `client/src/types/presentation.ts` - Client types

## Rules
- No two consecutive slides use the same layout
- Max 6 bullets per slide
- Theme: primaryColor, secondaryColor, fontTitle, fontBody, backgroundStyle
- Modern design: Use SlideChrome (header/footer), slide-modern-bg for subtle circles
